WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.582
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:09.304
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.604 --> 00:00:16.180
Unit four: Future Forms: Will and Going To. Today you will talk about plans, predictions and promises.

4
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.167
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.320
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.183 --> 00:00:24.894
Plan.

7
00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:28.301
Plan means something you have decided to do.

8
00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:30.452
I have a plan for Sunday.

9
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.366
Your turn. Say: Plan.

10
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.004
Plan.

11
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.658
Prediction.

12
00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.044
Prediction means a statement about the future.

13
00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.313
It is a weather prediction.

14
00:00:44.917 --> 00:00:47.290
Your turn. Say: Prediction.

15
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.123
Prediction.

16
00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:52.757
Promise.

17
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.481
Promise means a statement that you will do something.

18
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:58.398
I promise to help.

19
00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:01.380
Your turn. Say: Promise.

20
00:01:04.233 --> 00:01:05.234
Promise.

21
00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:06.880
Tomorrow.

22
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:09.987
Tomorrow means the day after today.

23
00:01:10.583 --> 00:01:12.374
I will call you tomorrow.

24
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:15.253
Your turn. Say: Tomorrow.

25
00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:19.182
Tomorrow.

26
00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:20.976
Next week.

27
00:01:21.983 --> 00:01:24.122
Next week means the week after this one.

28
00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.565
We are going to travel next week.

29
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.779
Your turn. Say: Next week.

30
00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:33.751
Next week.

31
00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:35.436
Probably.

32
00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:38.287
Probably means very likely.

33
00:01:38.883 --> 00:01:40.488
It will probably rain.

34
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:43.562
Your turn. Say: Probably.

35
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.308
Probably.

36
00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.005
Decide.

37
00:01:50.017 --> 00:01:52.074
Decide means to make a choice.

38
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:54.648
I have decided to study law.

39
00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:58.053
Your turn. Say: Decide.

40
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:01.936
Decide.

41
00:02:02.683 --> 00:02:03.510
Offer.

42
00:02:04.517 --> 00:02:07.166
Offer means to say you will do something for someone.

43
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.902
I'll carry your bag.

44
00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:11.797
Your turn. Say: Offer.

45
00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:15.588
Offer.

46
00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.981
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.817 --> 00:02:23.838
Visal, what is the difference between will and going to?

48
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:37.729
We use going to for plans and for predictions with evidence, for example, Look at those clouds! It is going to rain. We use will for quick decisions, offers, promises and general predictions.

49
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.387
Can you give examples?

50
00:02:41.483 --> 00:02:50.025
I am going to study medicine, because I have decided. The phone is ringing, so I'll answer it. I promise I will help you tomorrow.

51
00:02:51.117 --> 00:02:52.629
How do we make negatives?

52
00:02:53.717 --> 00:03:05.506
We say will not or won't, and am not, is not or are not going to. In questions we put will before the subject, and we put am, is or are before the subject with going to.

53
00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.167
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:09.017 --> 00:03:14.035
Grammar focus: Will plus base verb; be going to plus base verb.

55
00:03:14.335 --> 00:03:15.615
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:16.317 --> 00:03:19.082
I am going to study medicine because I have decided.

57
00:03:19.983 --> 00:03:22.122
The phone is ringing, so I'll answer it.

58
00:03:23.067 --> 00:03:29.713
Use going to for plans and evidence. Use will for quick decisions, offers, promises and general predictions.

59
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:34.661
Be careful! Don't say: It will rain! Look at the clouds.

60
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:39.786
Say: It is going to rain! Look at the clouds.

61
00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.819
Evidence needs going to.

62
00:03:42.633 --> 00:03:45.065
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:45.867 --> 00:03:47.413
Plans for the Holiday.

64
00:03:47.713 --> 00:03:50.549
Maly is going to visit her grandmother next week.

65
00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:53.428
She has already bought the bus ticket.

66
00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:57.188
Her brother says he will carry her bag to the station.

67
00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.490
The sky looks dark, so it is going to rain.

68
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.765
Maly promises she will send a message when she arrives.

69
00:04:05.867 --> 00:04:09.984
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.607
Look at those clouds! It blank rain.

71
00:04:13.907 --> 00:04:17.618
A, goes to. B, is going to. C, will not.

72
00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:23.584
The answer is B: is going to.

73
00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.205
The phone is ringing. I blank answer it.

74
00:04:27.505 --> 00:04:31.437
A, am going to. B, go to. C, will.

75
00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.825
The answer is C: will.

76
00:04:37.983 --> 00:04:39.228
Plans use blank.

77
00:04:39.528 --> 00:04:43.251
A, going to. B, will only. C, past simple.

78
00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.533
The answer is A: going to.

79
00:04:49.683 --> 00:04:51.706
What is Maly going to do next week?

80
00:04:52.006 --> 00:04:57.088
A, study abroad. B, visit her grandmother. C, buy a house.

81
00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.271
The answer is B: visit her grandmother.

82
00:05:04.417 --> 00:05:06.021
A promise uses blank.

83
00:05:06.321 --> 00:05:09.452
A, did. B, has. C, will.

84
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.941
The answer is C: will.

85
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:19.215
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.841
What are you going to do after the exam?

87
00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:32.150
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:43.209
I am going to rest for a few days and then visit my relatives in the province. I will also help my parents at home. I promise that I will keep studying English every day.

89
00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:45.172
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:52.776
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and will plus base verb; be going to plus base verb.

91
00:05:53.076 --> 00:05:57.087
Today's value is foresight. Prepare today for the world of tomorrow.

92
00:05:57.387 --> 00:05:59.888
See you in Unit five. Goodbye!

93
00:06:00.188 --> 00:06:03.247
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

